{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The 32GB memory card with an adapter fits my repeated use of SD and microSD cards, so it feels like a useful addition to equipment I already use.",
    "The Fire TV Cube offers a plausible next step for watching content on my television, although its 4K capability adds little for my 720p set."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The USB-C and Samsung tablet cables do not match my demonstrated connector needs; my Apple 30-pin cable does not imply a need for Samsung's different 30-pin connector.",
    "The SSD and NVMe enclosure suggest computer storage projects I have not shown interest in; my storage purchases have centered on removable memory cards.",
    "Photography accessories do not mean I want surveillance equipment, and owning a television and DVD player does not mean I am building a multichannel home theater.",
    "The Samsung tablet and keyboard lack a clear current purpose for me, while my tablet accessories have supported my existing Fire 7."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My electronics purchases seem to have been treated as interest in almost any electronic device, even when it serves a different purpose.",
    "Shared words such as camera, storage, tablet, and cable seem to matter more than whether an item works with my devices and supports what I actually do."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Exact device and connector compatibility matters because I often buy accessories to keep existing equipment useful.",
    "My repeated memory-card, tripod, reader, and cable purchases point toward practical additions and replacements more strongly than major equipment upgrades."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my memory-card needs and possible interest in TV streaming, but stretched my accessory purchases into unrelated devices and incompatible connections."
}"}
